## The Verdant Court

A court of fey held a glade deep in the [[Verdant Expanse]], where the forest is permanently dark. They are tall and gangly, with bluish-gray skin and limbs stretched longer than a person's. They wrap themselves in sheer gossamer cloth that looks too fine to have been made. Their faces are not faces: a bony growth covers the front of the head like a fused mask, and it opens to speak with a circular, lamprey-like mouth. Two horns rise from the top of the mask, and where eyes would be are empty black holes.

They serve a Lady whose court lies beyond a door. The two who held court in the glade were Oriel, who played a harp that the court's sing-song speech followed and whose melody could carve the door to their Lady, and Jin, who spoke for the rest and fought with thorns and confusion magic. Smaller ones sat in a ring around them and were called courtiers. A black raiment hangs over the two leaders, unlike any raiment of the Outer Gods the investigators knew, and unlike the green of the [[Green Father]].

They do not use names much among themselves and think the small folk give them out too freely. They know of the Green Father as something the "silly little ones outside" worship. A man passing through their wastes could come and go without their knowing him.

The court offered a choice: to entreat their Lady and end the curse, or to have the curse pointed at people of one's choosing. Ending it means entering the court through a door in a fallen tree, which Oriel's song carved into the bark as a rectangular door marked with a crescent moon. Jin said that entering would mean forsaking the [[Org/Iridescent Church/index|Iridescent Church]], and death.

Oriel, Jin and the courtiers of the glade are all dead.
